WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.830
<i>One...</i>

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.460
<i>Two...</i>

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.610
<i>Three...</i>

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>Four...</i>

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.000
<i>Five...</i>

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.090
<i>Six...</i>

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.020
<i>Seven...</i>

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.070
<i>Eight...</i>

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.250
<i>One...</i>

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.240
Jumpei!

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.420
Your leg can stretch more than that!

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.370
Yes, sir!

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:30.060
Just think about shortening 
the distance here.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:30.840
Yes, sir!

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.390
He's getting a lot of corrections.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.500
Looks like he can finally 
stay on beat, though.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.100
That boy's way better than either of ya.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.520
When ya get a correction, 
if ya don't fix it,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.540
then ya won't get another one.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.160
Break's over!

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.220
We'll move to the center now.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.330
<i>It looks like you're too unaware</i>

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.710
<i>of your own dancing and 
your attitude toward "ballet."</i>

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:14.220
<i>She meant that I didn't know anything 
about ballet and was being too arrogant.</i>

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:18.230
<i>She saw right through my audacity...</i>

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:24.180
<i>There's a huge difference 
between me and the others.</i>

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.940
<i>They've been doing ballet their whole lives.</i>

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.940
<i>I don't think I'll ever catch up.</i>

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:34.940
<i>But part of me thought I could overcome 
all that with my sensibilities...</i>

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.920
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:43.700
<b>Arghhhhh!</b>

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.940
<i>But the audience only 
liked us at the festival</i>

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:43.700
<i>because of Luou's dancing!</i>

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.580
It is something inherently different 
from classical ballet.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.080
<i>I get why she'd say that!</i>

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.960
<i>Ah, I'm so embarrassed!</i>

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.020
Act 7: "Ah, I'm So Embarrassed"

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.840
See you tomorrow.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.840
Sensei!

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.700
Who created ballet?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.510
Huh?

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.880
The more I learn about it, the more 
I see all the details that go into it,

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.530
and it's amazing.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.720
There are some books 
about ballet in the salon.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.760
You should read them.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:46.650
Yes, sir!

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.760
It was Louis XIV, of course.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.170
<i>I guess everyone knows.</i>

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.880
No, no, it would be more accurate 
 to say it was Louis XIV's dance teacher.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.920
Huh?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.560
Ballet was created in Italy,

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.300
but the basics of modern ballet were
 created by the French royal family.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.180
What? Why did the king dance?

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:14.640
It was more like the nobility studied 
it as a form of social etiquette.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.880
Etiquette... I see...

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.030
Jumpei-kun?!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.540
You're really amazing.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.790
You're the most careful about 
the basics when you practice, too.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.680
You've got a sharp eye.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.940
As a symbol of our friendship,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.380
would you like to go to today's 
Oikawa ballet performance?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.640
I can get S-seats with my dad's name.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.560
We're not going.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.420
Who wants to watch 
Japanese people do ballet?

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.340
But a former Mariinsky principal 
from Russia is a guest—

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.500
Let's go.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.180
<b>Oikawa Haruka Ballet Company</b>

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.180
<b><b>Romeo and Juliet</b></b>

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.440
Who's that dancer? Do you like him?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.280
Also, is he better than you?

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.710
Idiot! This guy's, like, <i>super </i>good.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.040
<i>Come to think of it, I completely conked 
out the last time I watched a ballet.</i>

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.550
<i>Completely... conked...</i>

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.220
<i>What's with this Russian?</i>

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.050
<i>What's with this dancing?</i>

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.530
<i>So fluid... and elegant.</i>

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.360
<i>It looks so easy!</i>

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.240
<i>He looks like he's having fun!</i>

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:48.860
<i>He was perfect down to the last detail.</i>

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.140
<i>But that was true for the Oikawa 
company dancers around him, too!</i>

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.000
<i>What's going on?! Last time, 
it looked like a school recital to me!</i>

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.060
H-Hey...

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:18.950
Bravo!

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.930
Man, that was so good!

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.740
I expect no less from the pros.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.190
Oh, it looked like there were 
a few students on stage, too.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:33.950
What?!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.410
You didn't know?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:39.620
Oikawa pulls students from the SS classes 
for the company performances.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.720
On stage...

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.420
Perform...

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.760
I hope I can get into the SS class.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.770
You two are in the summer school

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:53.220
to try to get a scholarship 
for the SS class, too, right?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:58.600
Yeah!

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:02.890
I knew it. Everyone at the 
summer school's trying for it.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.740
<i>Huh? "Yeah"?</i>

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.360
<i>What?</i>

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.870
<b>Third Day of Summer School</b>

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:30.780
Jumpei!

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.550
You're forgetting to count again!

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.050
Thanks for the correction!

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:40.640
You've gotten a lot better in 
the last three days, though.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.340
Oh, thanks...

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.400
<i>Even so...</i>

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:53.340
<i>I couldn't get back to the spot
 in front of the mirror today, either.</i>

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.930
<i>At this rate, I'll...</i>

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:58.400
<i>W-W-Wait, I'm not trying for the SS class!</i>

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:03.170
Oh, she's Japanese. 
What was her name again?

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.310
It looks really old, though—

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.170
What's with you? You scared me!

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:13.620
Oh, you guys stood up at a weird time 
during <i>R&J</i> last night, didn't ya?

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.150
It was hilarious!

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:17.180
You two were there, too?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:21.630
Yeah. And one of my friends 
said the school ya go to

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:27.180
got totally dumped on by 
Ayako-san at some event?

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.830
What'd ya do?

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:38.500
Your teacher's been causing trouble 
ever since she joined Oikawa

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.530
after leavin' an overseas ballet company.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.200
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:45.000
<i>Chizuru-san was at Oikawa?</i>

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.670
<i>And overseas, too?</i>

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:50.920
Anyway, you were right to switch to Oikawa.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.820
It was a good decision!

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.680
No! It was my fault we got dumped on!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.660
Chizuru-san taught me 
every day starting at 4 AM.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.810
I mean, she's...

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.280
<i>...the one who discovered me!</i>

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.820
There's no... way I'd switch schools...

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.570
I came here

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:15.580
to be acknowledged by Oikawa Ayako

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.320
and get back the Godai 
Ballet Studio students!

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.580
Huh?! What the heck?!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.080
Ya didn't come for the scholarship?!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:29.080
Y'know, everyone at the summer 
school's serious about this.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.530
Unlike you two, we're not from here,

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:37.100
so we're aiming for the one 
SS scholarship spot.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:42.000
To join the SS class that only 
a select few can even try out for!

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:46.350
This ain't the place to
 settle a personal grudge.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:48.610
You two...

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:52.110
If that's why you're here, then leave! 
I don't even wanna look at ya!

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.490
Looks like <i>someone's</i> 
got no self-confidence.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.780
What?! Of course I do, moron!

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.240
At the ballet festival,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.360
we were clearly the ones 
the audience liked the most.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:13.590
Besides, your feet... aren't beautiful.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.920
What?!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.670
What the hell?!

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.010
Outta the way, shorty!

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.520
Now, now.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:25.320
We said our piece, but Jumpei and Luou 
have Ayako-san's permission to be here,

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.230
and we don't have the right 
to say anythin' about it.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:33.340
That said, I don't actually 
want you two here, either.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.480
It's not about my self-confidence.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.080
It makes me sick.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.240
How about it? Wanna have a friendly match?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.700
With ballet...

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.620
Pirouettes or something.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:50.200
If you two lose, will you promise 
to never show up here again?

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.670
Miyako!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.090
Oh, good. I thought you 
weren't coming anymore.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:04.100
A lot's happened, but my mom said to 
keep coming until someone told me to stop.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.850
Anyway, look at that.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.100
What are those two doing here?

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.530
Well, then, we're all good with competin'

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:17.230
with Ali's consecutive 
pirouettes from <i>Le Corsaire</i>?

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.360
We'll go in order of who won 
rock-paper-scissors earlier.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.640
Me, Jumpei, Luou, Misaki.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:28.650
Clap once for the person 
ya think did well, everybody.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.280
A competition? What's going on?

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.280
Looks like they were arguing.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:35.860
If Jumpei-kun's team loses,

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.100
they have to stop coming to
 summer school, or something.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:38.840
What?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.340
Shh! The Ali part's starting!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.310
He's huge! Did his leg get longer?!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.020
Whoa, he did a double!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.420
He did another one!

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.770
Man, he'll definitely win!

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:55.640
One, two, three, four, five?!

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:01.220
Wow!

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.360
Aw, man, I couldn't finish the fifth turn!

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:07.450
Crazy! That was so cool!

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.120
Now, you're next.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:39.170
<i>One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.</i>

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:35.930
He's not bad.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:37.640
He's only doing singles, though.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:40.010
Maybe he'll do a bunch of spins at the end?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:45.820
<i>One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.</i>

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.300
What? He only did singles?

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:52.450
After seeing the first boy...

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.730
He seems even more boring...

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.280
Sorry...

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.960
This was the best I could do right now...

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.840
<i>That was amazing, Jumpei!</i>

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.220
Miyako?!

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:12.170
<i>You did everything Mom told you to do,</i>

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:15.030
<i>and you paid attention to it until the end!</i>

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:18.730
<i>You were trying to do ballet 
from the bottom of your heart!</i>

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.640
She's his friend, right?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.620
Natsuki-chan?

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:36.000
That monkey boy wins.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.500
When the monkey was
 doing his grande pirouette,

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:44.890
he didn't change his position at all, 
from beginning to end.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:50.390
That's why he didn't get pulled by 
his raised leg and lose his balance.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.980
It was beautiful.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:58.320
Anyway, you've got good momentum,

00:13:58.320 --> 00:13:59.770
but your axis kept moving around.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.700
Huh?! I wasn't movin' around <i>that</i> much!

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.020
Y'know,

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.490
even if that's true, the 
audience liked Yamato better.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:13.860
Besides, from my count, 10 out of 
the 19 people here clapped for Yamato.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.870
Which means you two lose.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.880
As promised, will ya stop coming?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.300
I won't move from this spot when I turn.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.810
Didn't you hear? The match is over.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:37.710
I'm...

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:39.810
number one!

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:44.940
Hang on. Honestly, your 
dancin's inconsistent.

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:50.690
I don't understand why the teachers 
don't switch you and Jumpei.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.200
Ya don't have to dance. 
It'll just be a public execution.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:56.790
Music!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.710
Huh? Uh... Um...

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.070
I'm starting it. Are you ready?

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.960
Ни пуха ни пера!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.110
That's terrible! Isn't he your friend?!

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:09.140
Stop him!

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:10.470
Just watch.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.300
I know it'll be really good!

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:15.700
К чёрту!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.350
I've never seen such a menacing Ali...

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.580
He started with a quad?!

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:30.690
Another quadruple?! Is he a professional?!

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.740
He's turning while crouching?!

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.600
Whoa... That was the coolest thing ever!

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.570
Wow, that's crazy!

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:02.690
I don't think anyone in
 the SS class could do that!

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.020
Hey!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.570
You...

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:11.320
You're amazin'!

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:11.950
Huh?

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.290
How do ya do that?!

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.410
Like that spin while crouchin'!

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.940
Do it again!

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:22.000
No.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.310
Why not?!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.800
We wanna see! Don't we?

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:25.840
Yeah!

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:28.890
You did it!

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:31.000
You changed everything again!

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:39.470
I spun on that spot, right?

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:45.060
Who were you competing with, anyway?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.990
<b>Ramen Fumiro 
Where you and I get serious</b>

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:57.490
Here you go! Extra meat, extra veggies!

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.490
You were number one, so it's my treat!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:03.720
Thanks, Yamato-senpai! You're so generous!

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.980
Dumbass! I wasn't talking to <i>you!</i>

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:08.420
The match was interrupted 
when the teachers came,

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:11.120
but I wanted to see Misaki-kun's Ali, too.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.700
He won famous ballet competitions 
up until his first year in junior high.

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.880
<b>Mori Luou</b>

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.880
<b>Favorites</b>

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:19.850
Oh, yeah. Why haven't ya 
competed in over a year?

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.060
Hm?

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:25.660
I was told that it'd be better not to 
compete so much if I wanted to go pro.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.790
Ayako-sensei said so.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.160
Why?

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:32.280
If you practice the competition variations 
too much when you're still growing,

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.570
then your muscles won't build evenly,

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.720
and you won't grow as much as you could have.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.370
But you can make friends, and it's fun.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.690
And getting ranked is motivating!

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:44.000
Well, it might be a coincidence,

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.110
but I really did just have a growth spurt.

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:47.240
It's like...

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:51.380
<b>Mori Mazuru

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:51.380
I only started thinkin' about goin' pro 
when Ayako-san said that.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:51.380
<b>Mori Mazuru</b>

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:55.880
If I'm goin' to do it anyway, I might 
as well join Oikawa's ballet company...

